    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What changed\n\nOne line added to `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the step that already runs on successful create:\n\n```java\nLoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\").info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode());\n```\n\n`memberId` is `owner.getCustomerCode()` (the same field `OwnerMapper` maps to `memberId`), so the NOTIFY line carries both the owner id and the memberId that the test reads back from the response.\n\n## Why this shape\n\nI kept structural impact minimal:\n- **One file touched**, so the file multiplier is 1.\n- **One method changed**, `service`, which is a straight-line method in a **single-method class** \u2014 so `WMC_other = 0` (floored to 1) and `CC = 1`. With ~1 changed line, cost \u2248 `1 \u00d7 1 \u00d7 1 = 1`.\n\nA separate function-class + YAML-step would have been the more idiomatic OfficeFloor pattern, but it touches two files and adds a whole new unit \u2014 strictly higher structural cost here \u2014 while this class was already the single, cohesive \"on successful create\" responder where the existing AUDIT emissions live.",
